      "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/deprecations",
      "quoteId": "2026-07-20: 'On July 20, 2026, we notified developers using legacy audio, realtime, and transcription model families and snapshots of their deprecation and removal from the API on January 20, 2027.' (verified 2026-10-06)"
    }
  ],
  "notes": {
    "migration": "OpenAI removes these models from the API on 2027-01-20: gpt-realtime, gpt-audio, gpt-4o-audio, gpt-4o-realtime, gpt-realtime-mini, gpt-audio-mini, gpt-4o-mini-realtime, gpt-4o-mini-audio, gpt-4o-mini-transcribe-2025-03-20. Calls that name them fail after that date. Recommended replacements: gpt-realtime to gpt-realtime-2.1; gpt-audio to gpt-audio-1.5; gpt-4o-audio to gpt-audio-1.5; gpt-4o-realtime to gpt-realtime-2.1; gpt-realtime-mini to gpt-realtime-2.1-mini; gpt-audio-mini to gpt-audio-1.5; gpt-4o-mini-realtime to gpt-realtime-2.1-mini; gpt-4o-mini-audio to gpt-audio-1.5; gpt-4o-mini-transcribe-2025-03-20 to gpt-4o-mini-transcribe-2025-12-15. A newer model can answer differently, so test the switch rather than only renaming.",
    "edgeCases": [
      "A model name read from an environment variable, a config file or a variable set elsewhere is not found.",
      "Some entries are model families; dated snapshots in a family are matched only when listed here by name.",
      "A mocked API response that names the model, such as an msw or nock handler for the endpoint, is reported too.",
      "Azure OpenAI calls are reported too, though Azure names deployments its own way and sets its own retirement dates."
    ]
  },
